      "side": 1,
      "message": "Linnan, thank you for sending the change and for sharing your thoughts with us.\n\nI think the highlighted part is the root of the problem.\nThe default value for `Message#what` is 0. When `what` is unspecified, such as when creating a `Message` to wrap a `Runnable`, it is 0.\nIf an app calls `Handler#removeMessages(0)` then I\u0027d say the behavior is not well-defined. This leads to the issues that you\u0027re seeing.\n\nSince `Message`, `Handler`, etc existed since API 1, we are very careful about making any behavior changes, even if they\u0027re not changes affecting a strictly defined contract.\n\nCould I propose adding documentation cautioning users about this issue as a possible alternative?\n\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/frameworks/base/+/3250153",
